From b51b0bd1c694171063a12601bbd68e9dbbe6eaef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ashallowperson <245951141+ashallowperson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 06:52:21 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] hal_neverallows: exempt hal_fingerprint_server from net_admin
 neverallow

The CM6 in-tree fingerprint AIDL HAL (jiiov) delivers its HBM capture
signal to the ANC engine via addressed kobject-uevent sendto, which the
kernel gates on CAP_NET_ADMIN (NL_NONROOT_SEND is unset for the
kobject-uevent family). As a proper halserverdomain member it now trips
the capability neverallow; exempt the public attribute following the
same pattern used for wifi/bluetooth/telephony HALs.
---
 private/hal_neverallows.te | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/private/hal_neverallows.te b/private/hal_neverallows.te
index c052d51d3..ede964b8c 100644
--- a/private/hal_neverallows.te
+++ b/private/hal_neverallows.te
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ neverallow {
   -hal_uwb_vendor_server
   -hal_nlinterceptor_server
   -hal_tv_tuner_server
+  -hal_fingerprint_server
 } self:global_capability_class_set { net_admin net_raw };
 
 # Unless a HAL's job is to communicate over the network, or control network
-- 
2.53.0

